openai/gpt-oss-120b,Female,"Some college, no degree",Conservative,31,1,"I think we need to crank up nuclear fast – it gives us steady power, good jobs, and cuts our reliance on foreign energy, without all the green‑talk drama.",3,The long-term hazards of radioactive waste disposal and the potential for catastrophic accidents are viewed as unacceptable risks to public safety and the environment.,"Look, we’ve been handling hazardous waste for decades—think of all the oil, coal ash, and chemicals we dump without a second thought, and nuclear’s waste is actually tracked, sealed in steel casks and stored in proven, secure facilities; plus, modern reactor designs have multiple fail‑safes that make catastrophic meltdowns practically impossible, so the “unacceptable risk” claim is more fear‑mongering than fact.","Investment in nuclear expansion is perceived as a diversion of critical resources away from more rapidly deployable, cost-effective, and safer renewable energy and storage technologies.","Look, renewables might be “quick” on paper, but they can’t reliably power our grid or replace the jobs that nuclear plants create—so throwing money at them just leaves us stuck with blackouts and higher bills. Investing in nuclear is the only way to get real, steady power now instead of chasing fantasies that never deliver."
