gemini-3-flash-preview,Male,Postgraduate,Conservative,16,1,"Nuclear energy provides the most reliable and efficient baseload power necessary for national energy independence and economic growth without the intermittency issues of subsidized renewables. Rapidly expanding our nuclear infrastructure is a pragmatic, high-tech solution to ensure a robust power grid and long-term domestic energy security.",3,The long-term hazards of radioactive waste disposal and the potential for catastrophic accidents are viewed as unacceptable risks to public safety and the environment.,"Statistically, nuclear power remains the safest energy source per megawatt-hour produced, and the perceived risks of waste are a manageable engineering challenge that modern recycling and containment technologies have already addressed. We cannot allow alarmist rhetoric regarding rare anomalies to derail a pragmatic strategy essential for our national energy security and long-term economic stability.","Investment in nuclear expansion is perceived as a diversion of critical resources away from more rapidly deployable, cost-effective, and safer renewable energy and storage technologies.","The claim that renewables are more cost-effective ignores the massive hidden costs of grid stabilization and the physical reality that intermittent sources cannot sustain a modern industrial economy. We must prioritize nuclear as the only proven, high-density power source capable of ensuring long-term national energy security and economic resilience."
