gemini-3-flash-preview,Male,Postgraduate,Moderate,74,1,"As an environmentalist focused on decarbonization, I believe rapid expansion of nuclear power is essential to provide the reliable, low-carbon baseload energy necessary to meet our climate goals and transition away from fossil fuels.",4,"Scientific investment is advocated to ensure that the transition away from fossil fuels is handled responsibly, avoiding the creation of a toxic legacy for future generations through improved safety and disposal standards.","While I agree that safety is paramount, we must ensure that the pursuit of perfect disposal standards doesn't become a bureaucratic barrier to the rapid deployment needed to halt the climate crisis. The ""toxic legacy"" of a warming planet is a far more immediate and catastrophic threat than the manageable risks of modern nuclear waste, making swift expansion the most responsible environmental choice.","Investment in nuclear expansion is perceived as a diversion of critical resources away from more rapidly deployable, cost-effective, and safer renewable energy and storage technologies.","While I appreciate the rapid scalability of renewables, they currently lack the long-duration storage necessary to maintain a stable grid on their own. We must view nuclear investment not as a diversion, but as the essential carbon-free foundation required to complement renewables and ensure a reliable, permanent transition away from fossil fuels."
